@page "/"
@using Sorcery.ServerSide.Components.Blogging;
@inject BlogBook BlogBook;

<PageTitle>Mat Gienieczko</PageTitle>

<MudContainer MaxWidth="MaxWidth.Large">
    <MudPaper Height="100%" Width="100%" Class="pa-sm-16 pa-4 my-4">
        <article>
            <Header1>Greetings!</Header1>
            <Paragraph>
                I'm Mateusz Gienieczko, a.k.a. V0ldek on all the platforms that allow you to put your nickname in.
                I'm a programmer and a researcher, currently pursuing a PhD at the Technical University of Munich at the
                Database Systems chair.
                You can learn more about me at <LinkA Href="/about">About me</LinkA> or at
                <LinkA Href="https://db.in.tum.de/people/sites/gienieczko/index.shtml?lang=en">the chair's website</LinkA>.
            </Paragraph>

            <Paragraph>
                I (try to) write a blog at <LinkA Href="/sourcery">Sourcery</LinkA>, here's the latest post:
            </Paragraph>

            <div class="ma-4">
                <BlogPostCard Post="BlogBook.Posts.First()"/>
            </div>

            <Paragraph>
                I have a course on C# starting from the very basics &ndash; check out <LinkA Href="/teaching">Teaching</LinkA>.
            </Paragraph>

            <Header2>About this page</Header2>
            <Paragraph>
                First of all, this page is fully open-source. If there are any issues that you see, or room
                for improvement and making it more accessible for you, please, file an issue on <LinkA Href="@GitHub.Sorcery">GitHub</LinkA>.
                I am the sole author of everything on this page, unless explicitly stated otherwise. I now explicitly state
                that the comments on this site are not necessarily mine, but I do moderate them.
            </Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>
                I use <LinkA Href="https://dotnet.microsoft.com/en-us/apps/aspnet/web-apps/blazor">Blazor</LinkA> and C#
                with the help of <LinkA Href="https://mudblazor.com/">MudBlazor</LinkA> components to make the site look good;
                then, it all gets turned into statically rendered files with
                <LinkA Href="https://github.com/ZarehD/AspNetStatic">AspNetStatic</LinkA> so that it loads fast and nice.
                I try to keep dependencies to a minimum, but I use
                <LinkA Href="https://katex.org/">KaTeX</LinkA> for pretty math,
                <LinkA Href="https://prismjs.com/">Prism</LinkA> for syntax highlighting,
                and the <LinkA Href="https://asciinema.org/">Asciinema</LinkA> player libraries for animated terminal snippets.
            </Paragraph>
            <Header2>Privacy</Header2>
            <Paragraph>
                All resources are statically hosted with the exception of comments;
                the only external calls that this site makes are to the comment service.
                There is no trackers and I do not store any personal information.
                I know, complete avant-garde. I wish "Web 3.0" was this instead of whatever it's
                being sold as right now.
            </Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>
                Comments are powered by <LinkA Href="https://giscus.app/">giscuss</LinkA> and hosted on
                <LinkA Href="https://github.com/V0ldek/Sorcery/discussions">GitHub Discussions</LinkA>;
                you need a GitHub account to post a comment, and all the comment data is managed by GitHub
                according to <LinkA Href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement">their privacy policy</LinkA>.
                If you wish your comments disappeared from this site simply delete them from the relevant GitHub Discussion.
            </Paragraph>
        </article>
    </MudPaper>
</MudContainer>
